### I. Concurrency and idempotency requirements

Use transactional row locking and database constraints.

Three mandatory live TiDB tests:

**T-CONC-01 — Parallel start/resume**

- Prepare one eligible target/item.
- Launch 10 parallel start-or-resume requests.
- All successful requests must resolve to the same in-progress attempt.
- Exactly one `activity_attempts` row may be created.
- Exactly one corresponding in-progress state must exist.

**T-CONC-02 — Parallel deliberate retry**

- Prepare a completed or abandoned previous attempt.
- Launch 5 parallel explicit retry requests against the same target/item.
- At most one new in-progress attempt may be created.
- Other requests must receive the existing idempotent result or deterministic conflict.
- No duplicate attempt numbers or idempotency records may exist.

**T-CONC-03 — Session expiry and re-login resume**

- Create an in-progress attempt.
- Save multiple ordered turns.
- Expire or revoke the authentication session without changing the attempt.
- Authenticate the synthetic Student again.
- Call start-or-resume.
- Verify the same attempt ID is returned.
- Verify all saved turns remain intact and ordered.
- Verify no automatic abandonment occurred.

Also test concurrent turn submissions and idempotent completion where feasible.

