## 6. Acceptance Criteria

P2-06 is PASS only when:

### Attempt lifecycle
- Student can start an eligible assignment item.
- Repeated start/resume returns the same in-progress attempt.
- Student can retrieve all saved turns.
- Student can save new turns in deterministic order.
- Duplicate turn submissions are idempotent or safely rejected.
- Student can deliberately complete an in-progress attempt.
- Student can deliberately abandon an in-progress attempt.
- A new attempt requires explicit retry intent.
- Network interruption, browser closure, logout, and session expiration never auto-abandon attempts.
- Closed assignments preserve read-only semantics.

### Progress
- Progress updates occur in the same transaction as lifecycle changes.
- Retry does not double-count completion.
- Abandonment is not counted as completion or failure.
- Teacher progress views reflect persisted workflow state.
- No psychological or diagnostic inference is generated.

### Ownership and privacy
- Student can only access their own attempts and turns.
- Teacher can read attempts only for assigned classes.
- Co-teachers have read-only review access within assigned classes.
- Teacher cannot mutate attempts.
- Admin is blocked from individual attempts, turns, and progress.

### Support metadata
- Optional AAC/read-aloud support use is recorded only where supported by existing schema.
- Missing support metadata is neutral.
- No support-use ranking or weakness score exists.

### Concurrency
- T-CONC-01: 10 parallel start/resume requests create exactly one in-progress attempt.
- T-CONC-02: 5 parallel explicit retries create at most one new in-progress attempt.
- T-CONC-03: session expiry/re-login resumes the same attempt with every saved turn intact.
- Existing database unique guards and transaction semantics are verified.

### Live TiDB
- Real repositories and services execute against synthetic fixtures.
- Preflight and post-cleanup counts match.
- Zero residual synthetic rows remain.
- No pre-existing records are modified.

### Regression
- P2-01 through P2-05 regression tests pass.
- New service, route, security, and concurrency tests pass.
- TypeScript check passes.
- Production build passes.
- Database health remains HTTP 200.
- No schema/migration changes occurred.

If any live integration case cannot safely run, mark it `NOT RUN` and explain the exact limitation. Do not fabricate PASS.

